    {
      "id": "mg-inductance-2",
      "title": "Inductance calculations",
      "kind": "practice",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "q1",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "N": [
              100,
              200,
              400
            ],
            "mur": [
              1000,
              2000,
              5000
            ],
            "Acm": [
              1,
              2,
              4
            ],
            "l": [
              0.1,
              0.2,
              0.3
            ]
          },
          "prompt": "A toroidal coil has {{N}} turns on a core with $\\mu_r$ = {{mur}}, cross-section {{Acm}} cm² and mean path length {{l*100}} cm. Find its inductance.",
          "answer": "N^2*mur*4*pi*1e-7*Acm*1e-4/l",
          "unit": "H",
          "explanation": "$\\mathcal{R} = \\frac{\\ell}{\\mu_r\\mu_0A}$ = {{l}} / ({{mur}} × 4π×$10^{-7}$ × {{Acm*1e-4}}) = {{l/(mur*4*pi*1e-7*Acm*1e-4)||4}} A·t/Wb.\n$L = N^2/\\mathcal{R}$ = {{N^2}} / {{l/(mur*4*pi*1e-7*Acm*1e-4)||4}} = {{N^2*mur*4*pi*1e-7*Acm*1e-4/l|H}}."
        },
        {
          "id": "q2",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "N": [
              200,
              300,
              500
            ],
            "lc": [
              0.2,
              0.3,
              0.4
            ],
            "mur": [
              2000,
              3000
            ],
            "Acm": [
              4,
              6,
              9
            ],
            "g": [
              0.0005,
              0.001,
              0.002
            ]
          },
          "derived": {
            "A": "Acm*1e-4",
            "Rc": "lc/(mur*4*pi*1e-7*A)",
            "Rg": "g/(4*pi*1e-7*A)"
          },
          "prompt": "A {{N}}-turn coil is wound on a core with $\\ell_c$ = {{lc*100}} cm, $A$ = {{Acm}} cm² and $\\mu_r$ = {{mur}}, which has an air gap of {{g*1000}} mm (neglect fringing). Find the inductance.",
          "answer": "N^2/(Rc+Rg)",
          "unit": "H",
          "explanation": "$\\mathcal{R}_c$ = {{Rc||4}} A·t/Wb, $\\mathcal{R}_g = \\ell_g/(\\mu_0A)$ = {{Rg||4}} A·t/Wb, total {{Rc+Rg||4}} A·t/Wb.\n$L = N^2/(\\mathcal{R}_c+\\mathcal{R}_g)$ = {{N^2}} / {{Rc+Rg||4}} = {{N^2/(Rc+Rg)|H}}. (Without the gap it would be {{N^2/Rc|H}}.)"
        },
        {
          "id": "q3",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "L": [
              0.01,
              0.02,
              0.05,
              0.1,
              0.2
            ],
            "g": [
              0.0005,
              0.001,
              0.002
            ],
            "Acm": [
              2,
              4,
              6
            ]
          },
          "derived": {
            "R": "g/(4*pi*1e-7*Acm*1e-4)"
          },
          "prompt": "You need a {{L|H}} inductor. The core has an air gap of {{g*1000}} mm and cross-section {{Acm}} cm²; the gap reluctance is so much larger than the iron's that you may neglect the iron. How many turns are needed?",
          "answer": "sqrt(L*R)",
          "unit": "",
          "explanation": "$\\mathcal{R} \\approx \\mathcal{R}_g = \\frac{\\ell_g}{\\mu_0A}$ = {{R||4}} A·t/Wb. From $L = N^2/\\mathcal{R}$: $N = \\sqrt{L\\mathcal{R}}$ = $\\sqrt{ {{L}} \\times {{R||4}} }$ = {{sqrt(L*R)||4}}, so about {{round(sqrt(L*R))}} turns."
        },
        {
          "id": "q4",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "M": [
              0.01,
              0.02,
              0.05,
              0.1
            ],
            "I": [
              0.5,
              1,
              2,
              5
            ],
            "T": [
              0.0005,
              0.001,
              0.002,
              0.005
            ]
          },
          "prompt": "Two coils have a mutual inductance of {{M|H}}. The current entering the dotted end of coil 1 rises steadily from 0 to {{I}} A in {{T|s}}. Coil 2 is open-circuited. Find the voltage at its dotted terminal with respect to its other terminal during the rise.",
          "answer": "M*I/T",
          "unit": "V",
          "explanation": "With $i_2 = 0$: $v_2 = M\\frac{di_1}{dt}$ = {{M}} H × ({{I}} A / {{T|s}}) = {{M}} × {{I/T}} = {{M*I/T|V}}. It is positive at the dot, because $i_1$ enters the dot of coil 1 and is increasing."
        },
        {
          "id": "q5",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "L1": [
              0.1,
              0.2,
              0.5
            ],
            "L2": [
